        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for python-Django fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in python-Django:\n\n- CVE-2026-108147: Potential memory exhaustion in MultiPartParser\n  via base64-encoded file upload (bsc#1289340)\n- CVE-2026-111211: Potential log injection via unescaped geometry\n  form values (bsc#1289344)\n- CVE-2026-111362: Server-side request forgery via crs member of\n  GeoJSON geometries (bsc#1289345)\n- CVE-2026-113593: Potential exposure of private data via empty\n  and missing Vary headers (bsc#1289348)\n- CVE-2026-114582: Server-side request forgery via SpatialReference\n  string input (bsc#1289350)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
